{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792889866,"nonce":"jbF/7ysM3MZ7uRjtHc+fS2jjzuQ=","title":"Native handles never reach a collection","message":"A finalizer block (an HDLL's or a plugin's handle to native memory) charges nothing to the trigger, and an HDLL's hl_gc_alloc_gen of one is no safepoint, so a loop making small native handles never collects and their native memory stays. Ash fixed this in 7b0f4069: charge each MEM_KIND_FINALIZER block 4 KB of external pressure, and run a deferred collection at an HDLL's finalizer allocation.","files":null}]}